---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="AWD system overview">
  <h1>AWD system overview</h1>
  <p>This page distinguishes the two AWD architectures available in the 2021 S60 range. The illustration below represents the mechanical AWD layout used on applicable T5 AWD and T6 AWD models. It is not a parts diagram, hydraulic schematic, wiring diagram, or service procedure. Exact component names and configuration must be confirmed against VIN-specific Volvo service information.</p>

  <figure class="diagram drivetrain-diagram">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1040 590" role="img" aria-labelledby="awd-title awd-desc">
      <title id="awd-title">2021 S60 mechanical AWD and T8 electric AWD power paths</title>
      <desc id="awd-desc">Two separate schematic power paths. T5 and T6 mechanical AWD send engine torque through the transmission and power take-off, propeller shaft and rear drive unit. T8 sends gasoline engine torque to the front axle and battery electricity through power electronics to an electric rear axle drive motor.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="awd-arrow-blue" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 Z" fill="#07569a"/></marker>
        <marker id="awd-arrow-gold" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 Z" fill="#b8860b"/></marker>
      </defs>
      <rect x="18" y="18" width="1004" height="258" rx="16" fill="#f2f7fc" stroke="#c6d7e8" stroke-width="2"/>
      <rect x="18" y="296" width="1004" height="276" rx="16" fill="#fff9e9" stroke="#ead9a3" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="48" y="55" font-size="22" font-weight="700" fill="#082d55">T5 AWD / T6 AWD · MECHANICAL REAR DRIVE</text>
      <text x="48" y="333" font-size="22" font-weight="700" fill="#6b4d00">T8 RECHARGE · ELECTRIC REAR DRIVE (eAWD)</text>

      <!-- Mechanical AWD lane -->
      <g stroke="#07569a" stroke-width="3" fill="#ffffff">
        <rect x="48" y="94" width="150" height="92" rx="10"/>
        <rect x="244" y="94" width="158" height="92" rx="10"/>
        <rect x="450" y="94" width="150" height="92" rx="10"/>
        <rect x="648" y="94" width="160" height="92" rx="10"/>
        <rect x="856" y="94" width="136" height="92" rx="10"/>
      </g>
      <g fill="#123b60" text-anchor="middle">
        <text x="123" y="130" font-size="18" font-weight="700">Gasoline</text><text x="123" y="154" font-size="15">engine</text>
        <text x="323" y="130" font-size="18" font-weight="700">8-speed</text><text x="323" y="154" font-size="15">automatic</text>
        <text x="525" y="130" font-size="18" font-weight="700">Front</text><text x="525" y="154" font-size="15">differential / axle</text>
        <text x="728" y="130" font-size="18" font-weight="700">PTO + prop</text><text x="728" y="154" font-size="15">shaft</text>
        <text x="924" y="130" font-size="18" font-weight="700">Rear drive</text><text x="924" y="154" font-size="15">unit / axle</text>
      </g>
      <g stroke="#07569a" stroke-width="4" fill="none" marker-end="url(#awd-arrow-blue)">
        <path d="M198 140 H244"/><path d="M402 140 H450"/><path d="M600 140 H648"/><path d="M808 140 H856"/>
      </g>
      <text x="520" y="224" text-anchor="middle" fill="#315a7d" font-size="15">Engine torque drives the front axle and is mechanically routed rearward through the AWD driveline.</text>

      <!-- T8 lane -->
      <g stroke="#b8860b" stroke-width="3" fill="#ffffff">
        <rect x="48" y="382" width="150" height="92" rx="10"/>
        <rect x="244" y="382" width="158" height="92" rx="10"/>
        <rect x="450" y="382" width="150" height="92" rx="10"/>
        <rect x="244" y="490" width="158" height="60" rx="10"/>
        <rect x="648" y="382" width="160" height="92" rx="10"/>
        <rect x="856" y="382" width="136" height="92" rx="10"/>
      </g>
      <g fill="#5d470d" text-anchor="middle">
        <text x="123" y="418" font-size="18" font-weight="700">Gasoline</text><text x="123" y="442" font-size="15">engine</text>
        <text x="323" y="418" font-size="18" font-weight="700">Automatic</text><text x="323" y="442" font-size="15">transmission</text>
        <text x="525" y="418" font-size="18" font-weight="700">Front</text><text x="525" y="442" font-size="15">drive axle</text>
        <text x="323" y="514" font-size="16" font-weight="700">High-voltage battery</text>
        <text x="728" y="418" font-size="18" font-weight="700">Power</text><text x="728" y="442" font-size="15">electronics</text>
        <text x="924" y="418" font-size="18" font-weight="700">ERAD</text><text x="924" y="442" font-size="15">rear electric motor</text>
      </g>
      <g stroke="#b8860b" stroke-width="4" fill="none" marker-end="url(#awd-arrow-gold)">
        <path d="M198 428 H244"/><path d="M402 428 H450"/>
        <path d="M402 520 H550 V475 H728 V474 H856"/>
      </g>
      <text x="520" y="560" text-anchor="middle" fill="#7a5d14" font-size="14">The rear axle is driven electrically; this is not the mechanical PTO / propeller-shaft layout.</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>Architecture comparison only. Boxes show functional relationships, not physical component locations, wiring, torque split, or service instructions.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>How the 2021 variants differ</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>T5 FWD:</strong> front-wheel drive; no rear propeller shaft or rear drive unit.</li>
    <li><strong>T5 AWD and T6 AWD:</strong> mechanical AWD layout represented by the diagram.</li>
    <li><strong>T8 Recharge:</strong> plug-in hybrid; the gasoline engine drives the front axle and an electric motor drives the rear axle. This is not the same parts layout as mechanical AWD.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note"><strong>Important:</strong> Do not use the mechanical AWD diagram to identify T8 components, and do not order AWD parts from the badge alone. Confirm the powertrain and VIN-specific component application.</p>

  <h2>What this diagram does not establish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Exact transmission model, gear ratios, or fluid specification.</li>
    <li>Exact angle-gear, coupling, or rear-drive-unit part numbers.</li>
    <li>Fluid capacities, service intervals, or torque values.</li>
    <li>Control-module wiring or diagnostic test points.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Volvo references</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.volvocars.com/is/support/car/s60-recharge-plug-in-hybrid/20w46/article/b0804d54c7fc096bc0a81f6f065ad63e/8899be1dc7fc78b1c0a81f6f5a01b4ab/00d308891f0cc443c0a80151619a46e9/">Volvo — 2021 S60 Recharge engine specifications</a>. Volvo identifies the electric rear axle drive (ERAD) as the rear electric drive motor; the page also notes market-specific engine availability.</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.volvotechinfo.com/">Volvo Technical Information</a> — VIN-specific service and diagnostic procedures.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For any repair, use the VIN-specific service procedure and confirm the component physically fitted to the vehicle.</p>
</BaseLayout>
